00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.202
to create a wisdom-based economy

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:22.341
that actually serves the needs of society.

00:00:22.341 --> 00:00:24.404
By learning to reawaken your creativity,

00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:27.901
you will recapture the natural enthusiasm,

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.179
energy, and wonder of youth.

00:00:30.179 --> 00:00:32.182
- He's an author and public speaker.

00:00:32.182 --> 00:00:34.804
He's a prominent figure
in the New Age movement.

00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:35.748
Through his books and videos,

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:37.313
he's become one of the most well known

00:00:37.313 --> 00:00:39.788
and wealthiest figures
in alternative medicine.

00:00:39.788 --> 00:00:41.560
He's Deepak Chopra, and here is my take

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.623
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:43.623 --> 00:00:45.350
Rule number 10 is my personal favorite,

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.999
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:49.416
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:55.250
- What we see, what we
perceive, what we hear,

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:57.805
what we think, what we imagine,

00:00:57.805 --> 00:01:00.888
what we understand, what inspires us.

00:01:02.876 --> 00:01:05.376
All of that comes from belief.

00:01:06.222 --> 00:01:09.889
And then these beliefs
project as our world.

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:13.577
We actually create the world

00:01:14.966 --> 00:01:17.966
that comes from these inner beliefs.

00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:21.872
In turn, the world feed backs at us.

00:01:21.872 --> 00:01:24.105
The world feeds back on us,

00:01:24.105 --> 00:01:27.846
and it reinforces what
we already believe in.

00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:32.013
So we see what we become, and
the world becomes who we are.

00:01:33.172 --> 00:01:37.350
If you talk to greatliness and
this is well done research,

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.754
even by Jim Collins if you read his book.

00:01:40.754 --> 00:01:44.226
He says that every leader in the end says

00:01:44.226 --> 00:01:46.284
one of the following things.

00:01:46.284 --> 00:01:50.307
"I was lucky" or "I happened
to be in the right place

00:01:50.307 --> 00:01:51.892
at the right time".

00:01:51.892 --> 00:01:54.493
"There were a lot of
meaningful coincidences."

00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:57.548
Now if they happen to be
spiritual or religious,

00:01:57.548 --> 00:02:01.420
they may use expressions
like "God was on my side",

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:03.420
"I seemed to be guided."

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:07.716
"There was a state of grace at times."

00:02:07.716 --> 00:02:09.931
"I was being looked after."

00:02:09.931 --> 00:02:13.175
What they're tapping into
is a deeper intelligence

00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:15.713
that goes beyond the personal.

00:02:15.713 --> 00:02:17.607
You might call it transpersonal,

00:02:17.607 --> 00:02:20.708
as the transpersonal
psychologists call it.

00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:22.771
Or you might call it archetypal,

00:02:22.771 --> 00:02:26.899
if you're familiar with
the teachings of Carl Jung.

00:02:26.899 --> 00:02:31.066
But what they do is they have
a relationship with a story.

00:02:32.477 --> 00:02:35.764
That's what a good brand is, by the way.

00:02:35.764 --> 00:02:38.339
A brand is an archetypal story.

00:02:38.339 --> 00:02:40.011
It has themes in it.

00:02:40.011 --> 00:02:42.314
The good guys, the bad guys.

00:02:42.314 --> 00:02:45.007
There's a little big of intrigue.

00:02:45.007 --> 00:02:47.935
There's mystery, there's adventure.

00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:52.061
All the ingredients that make
a really good soap opera.

00:02:52.061 --> 00:02:55.599
They have a relationship with that.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:58.360
A good brand is something that you'll buy

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.877
or use the service of when
you're actually buying the story.

00:03:02.877 --> 00:03:04.214
Apple is a story.

00:03:04.214 --> 00:03:06.214
It's a very great story.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:11.847
All the big brands, Nikes
shoes, it's the story

00:03:11.847 --> 00:03:14.631
of the African-American urban hero.

00:03:14.631 --> 00:03:18.267
One of the things I
tell leaders to do is...

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.777
What's your story?

00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:22.657
Can you make your story emotionally

00:03:22.657 --> 00:03:24.824
and spiritually inspiring?

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:29.777
People will buy your story as the brand,

00:03:29.777 --> 00:03:32.348
as the service, as the product.

00:03:32.348 --> 00:03:36.331
Follow your bliss does not
mean get addicted to pleasure.

00:03:36.331 --> 00:03:41.084
Follow your bliss means
finding the core of passion

00:03:41.084 --> 00:03:43.251
and excellence within you.

00:03:44.245 --> 00:03:47.963
It is to pursue excellence
and ignore success.

00:03:47.963 --> 00:03:51.891
If you do that, of course,
success will be a byproduct,

00:03:51.891 --> 00:03:56.058
but you're expressing the highest
potential within yourself.

00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:01.998
And when you do that,
you lose track of time,

00:04:01.998 --> 00:04:06.165
you experience ecstasy,
and when you express that,

00:04:08.152 --> 00:04:12.796
there's a need in society for
that particular expression.

00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:16.160
When society sees that, it honors you.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.618
It makes you a hero.

00:04:18.618 --> 00:04:21.242
The biggest challenge for all businesses

00:04:21.242 --> 00:04:23.483
is to restore real business.

00:04:23.483 --> 00:04:27.566
The economic meltdown was
something that happened

00:04:29.837 --> 00:04:33.920
because we had lost the
true purpose of business.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.682
What's the true purpose of business?

00:04:37.682 --> 00:04:40.180
Even in business school,
it's not well defined.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.434
They say the purpose of business

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:45.127
is to increase shareholder value.

00:04:45.127 --> 00:04:47.241
That's a ridiculous thing.

00:04:47.241 --> 00:04:50.824
The purpose of business
is to help society,

00:04:53.111 --> 00:04:54.954
to serve the needs of society.

00:04:54.954 --> 00:04:58.771
The purpose of business
is to serve the interests

00:04:58.771 --> 00:05:02.104
of all that are considered stakeholders.

00:05:03.085 --> 00:05:07.277
That includes the community
and the larger ecosystem.

00:05:07.277 --> 00:05:11.131
We created an economy, which
was based on spending money

00:05:11.131 --> 00:05:14.773
that people had not earned
to buy things that they

00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:18.666
did not need to impress
people that they did not like.

00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:22.053
Of the $2.9 trillion that are circulating

00:05:22.053 --> 00:05:25.825
in the world's markets,
less than two percent

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:29.919
was going to provide goods and services.

00:05:29.919 --> 00:05:34.217
The rest was what they
called derivatives, casino.

00:05:34.217 --> 00:05:37.544
So now for the first time, I
think we have the opportunity

00:05:37.544 --> 00:05:40.161
to create a wisdom-based economy

00:05:40.161 --> 00:05:43.622
that actually serves the needs of society.

00:05:43.622 --> 00:05:45.960
If you are a businessman today,

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:48.674
you need to totally reinvent yourself.

00:05:48.674 --> 00:05:52.452
You need to ask yourself what
are the wisdom-based economies

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.619
that I can participate in.

00:05:55.736 --> 00:06:00.223
The green economies, the
alternative energies.

00:06:00.223 --> 00:06:02.544
People who are planting trees

00:06:02.544 --> 00:06:05.627
are making a lot of money these days.

00:06:07.962 --> 00:06:09.649
You have to create an economy

00:06:09.649 --> 00:06:13.399
that is based on serving
the needs of people.

00:06:15.179 --> 00:06:16.899
The question that was asked was

00:06:16.899 --> 00:06:20.149
how do we maximize the use of our time.

00:06:21.575 --> 00:06:25.098
Here's my answer, and I learnt
this from Dr. Daniel Siegel,

00:06:25.098 --> 00:06:27.015
a UCLA psychotherapist.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:32.922
He says divide time in 24 hours
into the following sections.

00:06:35.235 --> 00:06:38.818
Sleep time, meditation
time, exercise time,

00:06:40.612 --> 00:06:44.779
relationship time, downtime,
creative and playtime,

00:06:46.147 --> 00:06:49.147
focused work time, and when you eat.

00:06:51.157 --> 00:06:53.497
And when you're doing
each of these things,

00:06:53.497 --> 00:06:55.062
then just do those things.

00:06:55.062 --> 00:06:56.868
Don't do anything else.

00:06:56.868 --> 00:06:58.637
I thought that was very brilliant,

00:06:58.637 --> 00:07:02.837
and I've been doing this
now for a number of years.

00:07:02.837 --> 00:07:06.315
I sleep at least six to eight hours a day.

00:07:06.315 --> 00:07:08.698
I meditate early in the morning

00:07:08.698 --> 00:07:11.442
for about one and one-half hours.

00:07:11.442 --> 00:07:13.701
I go to the gym after that.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:16.868
I walk between five to 10 miles a day.

00:07:18.548 --> 00:07:21.798
I work from about 9 o'clock to 12 noon.

00:07:23.095 --> 00:07:26.345
I take a full hour for a mindful lunch.

00:07:27.937 --> 00:07:30.902
I take a 20-minute walk after lunch.

00:07:30.902 --> 00:07:34.491
Then I start working
again in the afternoon

00:07:34.491 --> 00:07:37.741
around 1 o'clock or so, 1:30, two even.

00:07:40.897 --> 00:07:44.875
Then I do a short meditation
at 4:30 in the evening,

00:07:44.875 --> 00:07:48.963
5 o'clock, and I have an
early supper around six,

00:07:48.963 --> 00:07:51.213
and I'm in bed by about 10.

00:07:53.191 --> 00:07:55.245
Now when I'm doing this daily routine,

00:07:55.245 --> 00:07:58.329
then I feel that my rhythms are in order.

00:07:58.329 --> 00:08:02.246
They're connected to the
rhythms of the cosmos.

00:08:03.272 --> 00:08:07.196
When I'm speaking to someone,
I'm present with them.

00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:11.043
I don't check my iPhone
or my hand-held device

00:08:11.043 --> 00:08:13.426
at the same time, because
the cortical brain

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:16.135
can only do one thing at a time.

00:08:16.135 --> 00:08:19.380
So, of course, the
autonomic nervous system

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.049
can do many things at a time.

00:08:22.049 --> 00:08:26.398
Do one thing, do it
mindfully, and do it well.

00:08:26.398 --> 00:08:29.927
Pursue excellence and ignore success.

00:08:29.927 --> 00:08:34.094
Stay detached and divide your
time into those quadrants.

00:08:35.338 --> 00:08:38.078
- So apart from running
out and creating a story,

00:08:38.078 --> 00:08:41.206
what can the viewers, right
now, do today or tomorrow

00:08:41.206 --> 00:08:42.896
to make themselves better leaders?

00:08:42.896 --> 00:08:45.307
- First, ask yourself those
questions that I mentioned.

00:08:45.307 --> 00:08:47.561
Who am I, what do I
want, what kind of team

00:08:47.561 --> 00:08:49.814
do I want to have, what's my role in it,

00:08:49.814 --> 00:08:52.067
what are my skills and strengths,

00:08:52.067 --> 00:08:55.596
what are the skills and
the strengths of the people

00:08:55.596 --> 00:08:58.184
that I want to have on my team?

00:08:58.184 --> 00:09:01.517
If people are not being fully expressive

00:09:03.035 --> 00:09:07.083
in their unique strengths,
they lose self-esteem.

00:09:07.083 --> 00:09:09.150
If they're not having fun.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:13.113
I am also a senior scientist
at Gallup Organization,

00:09:13.113 --> 00:09:17.289
and we find that only 20%
of people in this country

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:19.638
are engaged in what they do.

00:09:19.638 --> 00:09:23.326
About 15 to 20% are actively disengaged.

00:09:23.326 --> 00:09:26.248
They come to work unhappy,
and they make it a point

00:09:26.248 --> 00:09:29.004
of making other people unhappy.

00:09:29.004 --> 00:09:31.423
The rest are kind of
punching in the clock.

00:09:31.423 --> 00:09:36.397
This costs our economy something
like $380 billion a year.

00:09:36.397 --> 00:09:40.564
So what makes a fun, invigorating
productive environment?

00:09:41.777 --> 00:09:45.929
Well, if your supervisor
or manager ignores you,

00:09:45.929 --> 00:09:49.665
your rate of disengagement goes up by 45%.

00:09:49.665 --> 00:09:53.355
If the supervisor or
manager doesn't ignore you

00:09:53.355 --> 00:09:56.183
but criticizes you,
your rate of engagement

00:09:56.183 --> 00:09:57.515
drops to 20%.

00:09:57.515 --> 00:09:59.469
You would rather be criticized

00:09:59.469 --> 00:10:01.971
because you are now being noticed.

00:10:01.971 --> 00:10:05.216
On the other hand, if your
manager notices a single strength

00:10:05.216 --> 00:10:08.256
that you have, your rate
of disengagement falls

00:10:08.256 --> 00:10:10.299
to less than one percent.

00:10:10.299 --> 00:10:13.294
This has huge economic implications.

00:10:13.294 --> 00:10:17.361
Each of us is born as an
infinitely creative being.

00:10:17.361 --> 00:10:20.519
As children, we use our rich imaginations

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.497
to create entire worlds,

00:10:22.497 --> 00:10:25.781
whether we were building
sandcastles at the beach,

00:10:25.781 --> 00:10:28.531
playing house with a collection of dolls,

00:10:28.531 --> 00:10:31.945
or pretending to be
our favorite superhero.

00:10:31.945 --> 00:10:34.820
But as we become adults,
many of us succumb

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.462
to the prevailing
cultural meme, or belief,

00:10:38.462 --> 00:10:42.205
that the older we get, our
brains lose their capacity

00:10:42.205 --> 00:10:45.538
to expand, adapt, transform, and evolve.

00:10:46.666 --> 00:10:47.899
But it's a lie.

00:10:47.899 --> 00:10:50.492
As numerous studies have discovered,

00:10:50.492 --> 00:10:54.551
the brain has a quality
referred to as plasticity.

00:10:54.551 --> 00:10:57.548
The ability to form new neural pathways

00:10:57.548 --> 00:10:59.465
even into very old age.

00:11:00.863 --> 00:11:04.995
The brain is fluid, flexible,
and incredibly adaptable

00:11:04.995 --> 00:11:06.532
to new experiences.

00:11:06.532 --> 00:11:10.832
Neuroplasticity is what
allows us to teach ourselves

00:11:10.832 --> 00:11:14.473
a new language, learn to play the piano,

00:11:14.473 --> 00:11:18.827
play a new sport, or learn
the latest dance move.

00:11:18.827 --> 00:11:20.886
Although you may no
longer think of yourself

00:11:20.886 --> 00:11:23.965
as a creative or imaginative person,

00:11:23.965 --> 00:11:28.132
your very existence is evidence
of your innate creativity.

00:11:29.392 --> 00:11:32.505
In every moment, you are
co-creating your reality

00:11:32.505 --> 00:11:35.520
through your thoughts, your intentions,

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.957
your words, and your actions.

00:11:37.957 --> 00:11:41.063
We all have unlimited creative potential

00:11:41.063 --> 00:11:45.197
because our essential nature
is pure consciousness.

00:11:45.197 --> 00:11:47.660
By learning to reawaken your creativity,

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.836
you will recapture the natural enthusiasm,

00:11:50.836 --> 00:11:53.167
energy, and wonder of youth.

00:11:53.167 --> 00:11:56.373
As the ancient vedic
sages of India observe,

00:11:56.373 --> 00:11:58.385
the secret of immortality

00:11:58.385 --> 00:12:02.410
is infinite flexibility and creativity.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:06.150
A victim of conditioning means
that your habitual patterns

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:10.317
of behavior and thinking are
result of the collective psyche

00:12:15.562 --> 00:12:18.938
and what we call normal
in the collective psyche

00:12:18.938 --> 00:12:22.582
is actually the
psychopathology of the average.

00:12:22.582 --> 00:12:26.737
Dull, ordinary, mundane,
always looking for fulfillment

00:12:26.737 --> 00:12:28.394
on something outside.

00:12:28.394 --> 00:12:30.964
If I had the right job
or had the right money,

00:12:30.964 --> 00:12:33.055
if I had the right relationship

00:12:33.055 --> 00:12:36.960
Whatever the right thing
then I'd be a happy person.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:38.399
But it's the other way around.

00:12:38.399 --> 00:12:39.881
If you're happy, you'll
have the right job,

00:12:39.881 --> 00:12:42.643
you'll have the right money
and have the right success.

00:12:42.643 --> 00:12:44.419
You'll make the right
choices for your health

00:12:44.419 --> 00:12:46.852
and you'll have the right relationships.

00:12:46.852 --> 00:12:49.274
- A lot of people don't
really relate business

00:12:49.274 --> 00:12:50.719
and spirituality together.

00:12:50.719 --> 00:12:52.078
You don't really hear about it.

00:12:52.078 --> 00:12:53.762
How do you think it does work though?

00:12:53.762 --> 00:12:55.922
Do you think you need that part?

00:12:55.922 --> 00:12:58.587
- I define spirituality as self-awareness

00:12:58.587 --> 00:13:02.754
and also as elements of
compassion, love, service,

00:13:04.297 --> 00:13:06.935
honesty, authenticity, integrity.

00:13:06.935 --> 00:13:10.576
I think even if you don't
relate to those values,

00:13:10.576 --> 00:13:13.935
if you incorporate those values,
your business will thrive.

00:13:13.935 --> 00:13:16.103
Ask yourself, what's your purpose.

00:13:16.103 --> 00:13:19.905
What kind of contribution
do you want to make?

00:13:19.905 --> 00:13:22.856
What creates joy and ecstasy in you?

00:13:22.856 --> 00:13:26.210
What are the two or three
skills that you have

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:30.298
that when you're expressing
your unique talents and skills,

00:13:30.298 --> 00:13:32.511
time means nothing to you?

00:13:32.511 --> 00:13:34.470
It's not work, it's joy?

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:38.205
Ask yourself who are
your heroes and heroines

00:13:38.205 --> 00:13:41.335
in history and mythology and religion,

00:13:41.335 --> 00:13:44.986
because these are
archetypes that are seeking

00:13:44.986 --> 00:13:49.153
to find expression through
you and incarnate through you.

00:13:51.449 --> 00:13:54.281
Ask yourself how can this passion of mine

00:13:54.281 --> 00:13:56.531
contribute to relationship?

00:13:58.464 --> 00:14:01.544
Give meaning and purpose to existence?

00:14:01.544 --> 00:14:03.435
You don't need to know the answers.

00:14:03.435 --> 00:14:07.006
If you live the questions, then
life has an interesting way

00:14:07.006 --> 00:14:09.589
of moving you into the answers.

00:14:11.479 --> 00:14:12.797
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:14:12.797 --> 00:14:15.507
I made this video because
Calavera Magna asked me to.

00:14:15.507 --> 00:14:16.983
